  {
   "id": "S1HOQawYAwAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2019-06-29T18:06:39Z",
   "subject": "Re: measEq.syntax() Error in TEST[[2]] : subscript out of bounds",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div lang=\"PT\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif\">or if it’s just a problem with sample size (n=390, second order factor with 15 ordinal items, 8 groups) and polychoric correlation estimation…</span></p></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>You have divided n=390 into 8 groups?!  That is a small sample even for a single-group model with DWLS estimation.  And dividing into 8 groups (at best, your smallest n = 390/8 &lt; 50) means the samples would be too small even with multivariate normal indicators.</div><div><br></div><div>Sorry, but sometimes you just need to accept that you do not have the data needed to test a hypothesis with any kind of justified confidence.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423477629000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1hUcoqXk_m8roYH_5W4x2X\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
